# VTID-03683 — commands run, in order
#
# Everything below is local (tests, typecheck, mutation) plus read-only
# production SELECTs. No production write, no ORB session started, no deploy.

# --- dependency ---
npm install @aws-sdk/client-transcribe-streaming --save
#   → services/gateway/package.json + package-lock.json
#   NOTE: the lockfile change is unavoidable and trips VALIDATOR-CHECK exit 20.
#   See acceptance.md "Dependency note".

# --- typecheck, after each file was added ---
npx tsc --noEmit
#   → exit 0, clean. No `as never` / `as any` casts remain in the new code.
#   Two real bugs were caught here rather than at runtime:
#     1. `callViaRouter` opts field is `systemPrompt`, not `system`. An earlier
#        draft passed `system` behind an `as never` cast — it compiled, and
#        would have silently DROPPED the entire system instruction, leaving a
#        generic assistant that sounded fine and knew nothing.
#     2. required `service` field was missing from the same call.
#   Also caught: two sites in routes/orb-live.ts re-declared the provider union
#   locally as 'vertex'|'livekit'|'nova_sonic'; without updating them they would
#   have silently excluded 'cascaded'.

# --- new suite ---
npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/cascaded-voice.test.ts
#   → 11 passed, 11 total. See outputs/tests.txt

# --- verifying the Transcribe language codes against the SDK, not against a guess ---
grep -A60 'declare const LanguageCode' \
  node_modules/@aws-sdk/client-transcribe-streaming/dist-types/models/enums.d.ts
#   → confirms SR_RS: "sr-RS" exists, i.e. Serbian's blocker is Polly ONLY.
#   This is why the eligibility check consults Polly BEFORE Transcribe: so the
#   refusal reason names the service that is actually the blocker.

# --- mutation verification (3 seams) ---
# 1. remove the nova-native refusal   → 2 tests fail
# 2. remove the Polly coverage guard  → 3 tests fail
# 3. ignore the activation gate       → 1 test fails
# each restored from a copy taken beforehand; full detail in outputs/mutation.txt
npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/cascaded-voice.test.ts   # after each mutation

# --- full regression ---
npx jest
#   → first run: 1 failure, test/orb/live/upstream/provider-name.test.ts, which
#     pins VOICE_PROVIDER_NAMES as an EXACT list and correctly objected to the
#     new member. Updated to name all four and KEEP the exact-list form rather
#     than loosening it to toContain.
#   → after: 673/674 suites (1 pre-existing skip), 12940 passed, 0 failed.

